The Domain Controller answered 'name-to-IP' for lab.TracenAcademy.internal, I added a forwarder so it can pass public names to an
upstream resolver instead of accessing the internet root server. This will keep EntraID and system updates from not working. 
An reverse zone was for 172.16.156.0/24 was created to answer the 'IP-to-name' queries (https://www.cloudflare.com/learning/dns/dns-records/dns-ptr-record/)
for my DC's PRT record. Setting dynamic updates to secure ensures only domain members can register records.

Step 1: Check what is already there

Get-DnsServerForwarder
Get-DnsServerZone

A good rule of thumb is to know what already exists before changes are made.

Step 2: Tell the Domain Controller where to ask for outside names

Add-DnsServerForwarder -IPAddress 8.8.8.8 -PassThru

Since this is an internal lab, the DC only knows the address in the lab. For outside queries like google.com or umamusume.com,
the DC will now ask 8.8.8.8 (primary DNS server for Google)

Step 3: Create the reverse zone for my subnet

Add-DnsServerPrimaryZone -NetworkId "172.16.156.0/24" -ReplicationScope Domain -DynamicUpdate Secure

This step gives the DC the ability to turn that pesky IP back into a name

Step 4: Check the DC's own reverse record

Resolve-DnsName 172.16.156.10
(this should return the DC's name)

Step 5: Test outside names through the Domain Controller

Resolve-DnsName umamusume.com -Server 172.16.156.10
This will return the address

Step 6: Confirmation, Confirmation, Confirmation

Get-DnsServerZone -Name "156.16.172.in-addr.arpa" | Select-Object ZoneName, DynamicUpdate, ReplicationScope

Checking IsDsIntegrated for 'True' and DynamicUpdate is 'Secure'
